<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17520" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">factīcĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		facio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>made by art</i>, <i>artificial</i>, <i>factitious</i> (postAug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 7, 39, § 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 7, 42, § 91</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">35, 6, 24,
				§ 40</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ladanum (opp. terrenum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 17, 37, § 75</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			the later grammarians: nomen, <i>formed to imitate the
				natural sound</i>, <i>onomato - poetic</i>, like
			tintinnabulum, turtur, <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 581</span></i>
			P.</div>
